# CODEOWNERS — approval-boundary gate for the babelstone monorepo.
#
# Enforces the three-owner configuration-surface split (01 §3, ADR-PC-019 F2):
# the cheapest, most frequent change must not inherit the most expensive approval.
# Every merge to a gated path requires its owner's review, so the segregation is a
# property of the merge gate, not of repository count.
#
# Team size note: at the current 1–2-person team the three config-surface roles
# (Product team / Treasury-ALM / Engine team + regulatory counsel) all resolve to
# @jhosm. Replace the per-role handle with a GitHub team (e.g. @jhosm-org/treasury)
# when the org adds the team; the role each line represents is named in its comment.

# --- Default owner -----------------------------------------------------------
*                       @jhosm

# --- Product-engine + in-house estate (engine team) --------------------------
/engine/                @jhosm
/pack-validate/         @jhosm
/families/              @jhosm
/contracts/             @jhosm
/orchestrator/          @jhosm
/acl/                   @jhosm
/mcp-server/            @jhosm
/notification/          @jhosm
/infra/                 @jhosm

# --- Three-owner configuration surface (01 §3) -------------------------------
# Product configs (structure)            — role: Product team
/product-configs/       @jhosm
# Rate sheets (numerical rates)          — role: Treasury / ALM
/rate-sheets/           @jhosm
# Pack (jurisdiction-scoped vocabulary)  — role: Engine team + regulatory counsel
/packs/                 @jhosm

# --- Docs & ADRs (engine team) -----------------------------------------------
/docs/                  @jhosm
